# Per-package USE flags — Orange Pi 3 LTS (Allwinner H6, arm64) headless
# appliance. Much shorter than the desktop platforms' equivalent file: with NO
# X11/GTK/browser stack at all, most of Frite/Orange-Pi-5's cross-compile-gap
# trims (rsvg/harfbuzz/libfm/pinentry-gtk/...) simply do not apply here — there
# is no gtk+/netsurf/lightdm in this platform's package set to trim USE flags on.

# gentoo-sources: install the source symlink so the kernel build can find it.
sys-kernel/gentoo-sources symlink

# parted needs device-mapper for the installer's partitioning helpers.
sys-block/parted device-mapper

# NetworkManager: keep wifi USE compiled in case a USB WiFi dongle with its OWN
# mainline driver is ever attached — the ONBOARD Unisoc UWE5622 radio
# has NO mainline driver at all (see the kernel fragment + README) and is not
# what this USE flag is for. rfkill-blocked + module-blacklisted by default
# regardless (harden_radios() in the builder).
net-misc/networkmanager wifi

# networkmanager modemmanager USE disabled: +modemmanager pulls modemmanager ->
# libqmi[qrtr] -> net-libs/libqrtr-glib -> dev-libs/gobject-introspection ->
# glib with introspection enabled. Cellular modems are absent from this SBC;
# disabling modemmanager has no functional impact. Mirrors
# specs-frite/specs-orangepi5's identical trim.
net-misc/networkmanager -modemmanager

# pinentry gtk USE disabled: +gtk causes pinentry to require app-crypt/gcr:4[gtk],
# which in turn requires gui-libs/gtk-4 (fails cross-configure) — and this
# platform has no GTK stack at all to make +gtk meaningful anyway. The ncurses/
# curses pinentry backend is sufficient for the rare interactive passphrase
# prompt (--encrypt-root install time).
app-crypt/pinentry -gtk
